# ALLOWLIST. Everything is ignored unless named below.
#
# This is deliberately inverted. A denylist protects only the paths you thought of, and
# would publish the next working directory the moment it was called something new, along
# with any brief or requirements document left in the repo root.
#
# pica ships the METHOD: rules, commands, hooks, scripts, the sector base, the checks.
# Working material is not content for anyone installing it, and it carries briefs, real
# copy and identifiers that are not redistributable. What survives it belongs in
# CHANGELOG.md, which is the durable form: a rule stated next to the failure that earned
# it, and nothing that identifies where the failure happened.
#
# To publish something new, add it here on purpose. If you find yourself adding a
# directory of work rather than a directory of method, that is the signal to stop.

/*

# ---- the plugin surface: this is what pica IS ----
!/.claude-plugin/
!/commands/
!/hooks/
!/packages/
!/skills/
!/scripts/

# ---- repo furniture ----
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE
!/.gitignore

# ---- the pipeline ----
# The allowlist ignored .github/ until 1.2.3, so the first ci.yml written here was
# silently not staged. It is the pipeline itself: nothing under it is working material.
!/.github/

# ---- README artwork, authored here and containing no project content ----
# SVG only, deliberately: it is text, so it diffs and reviews like source. Raster
# formats stay ignored below precisely because a screenshot is the easiest way to
# leak a client's screen into the repo without noticing.
!/assets/
/assets/*
!/assets/*.svg

# ---- docs: design specs and implementation plans, never brainstorm scratch ----
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/specs/
!/docs/plans/

# ---- belt and braces ----
# These are ignored at ANY depth, including inside an allowlisted directory, so a
# captured artefact or a client brief cannot ride along inside skills/ or docs/.
.pica/
.audit/
.cmp/
node_modules/
*.docx
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.sketch
*.fig

# ---- the worked example: the mutation suite's fixture ----
# Added on purpose, per the rule at the top of this file.
#
# scripts/mutate.mjs copies its fixture from examples/approvals. While that directory was
# ignored the suite ran on exactly one machine: a fresh clone got "examples/approvals is
# missing, and it is the fixture", so pica's central claim — every check has been seen to
# fail on the defect it was written for — was unverifiable by anyone else, CI included.
#
# This is method, not working material: a synthetic retail-bank approval surface authored
# here as the worked example the README points at. It carries no client brief and no real
# identifiers.
#
# The exceptions below are deliberately narrow, and must come AFTER belt-and-braces
# because the later rule wins. Exactly one hole is opened: .pica/state.json, which the
# checks read and without which the fixture is inert. .audit/ and every screenshot rule
# are left exactly as they were — the suite was measured at 89 caught · 0 missed with no
# .audit directory present at all, so publishing a captured screen is never the price of
# a working mutation suite.
!/examples/
/examples/*
!/examples/approvals/
!/examples/approvals/**
!/examples/approvals/.pica/
